# Ever2e C++

Ever2e is an Apple IIe emulator ported to a CMake-based C++ build. The repo
keeps source, profiles, samples, and tests in separate folders; local ROMs,
disk images, generated outputs, and archived legacy release files belong under
`local/`, which is intentionally ignored by git.

## Layout

- `src/`, `include/` - emulator source and headers grouped by domain:
  `app`, `cpu`, `devices`, `memory`, `platform`, and `video`.
- `profiles/apple2e.emu` - the default Apple IIe profile with no expansion
  cards installed.
- `samples/` - BASIC programs and manual smoke-test inputs.
- `tests/fixtures/` - committed data used by automated tests and scripts.
- `scripts/macos/` - build, run, and smoke-test helpers.
- `local/` - private workspace for ROMs, disk images, generated files, and
  archived files removed from the committed tree.

## Dependencies

Required:

- CMake 3.21 or newer
- A C++17 compiler
- SDL3 development libraries

Optional:

- FFmpeg development libraries for `--record-video`

On macOS:

```sh
brew install sdl3
```

## Build And Test

From the repository root:

```sh
cmake --preset macos-release
cmake --build --preset macos-release
ctest --preset macos-release
```

Platform presets:

- macOS: `macos-release`
- Linux: `linux-release`
- Windows: `windows-release`

The macOS helper builds the emulator and microcode tests:

```sh
./scripts/macos/build.sh
```

## Run

The emulator requires a positional `.emu` profile. The default helper profile is
`profiles/apple2e.emu`.

```sh
./scripts/macos/run.sh
./scripts/macos/run.sh --rom-file /absolute/path/to/APPLE2E.ROM
./build/macos/ever2e profiles/apple2e.emu --rom-file /absolute/path/to/APPLE2E.ROM
```

By default, `profiles/apple2e.emu` looks for a local ROM at
`local/roms/APPLE2E.ROM`. Apple II ROM images are not committed.

## Profile Overrides

Use `--set name=value` to override any `.emu` property after the profile is
loaded. `--set-property` is an alias. Path values support `~` expansion and are
resolved relative to the profile unless absolute.

Disk II drive image paths can be supplied per run:

```sh
./scripts/macos/run.sh \
  --rom-file /absolute/path/to/APPLE2E.ROM \
  --set machine.layout.slot.6.rom.file=/absolute/path/to/DISKII_P6.rom \
  --disk1 /absolute/path/to/disk.nib
```

`--disk1` and `--disk2` enable the slot 6 Disk II controller and override drive
1/2 image paths. A 256-byte slot ROM is still required with
`machine.layout.slot.6.rom.file`; the disk flags do not provide one.

## Automation Scripts

```sh
./scripts/macos/run_smoke.sh
./scripts/macos/run_p6_boot_smoke.sh
./scripts/macos/run_trace_baseline.sh
./scripts/macos/run_main_tests.sh
./scripts/macos/run_microcode_tests.sh
./scripts/macos/run_generated_tests.sh
```

Useful environment overrides:

- `ROM_FILE=/absolute/path/to/APPLE2E.ROM`
- `ROM_GENERATED=loop` for scripts that support a temporary loop ROM
- `EMU_FILE=/absolute/path/to/profile.emu`
- `STEPS=120000000`
- `REBUILD_ON_RUN=0`

`run_p6_boot_smoke.sh` is proprietary-free: it generates a temporary slot-6 ROM,
custom boot disk, and wrapper ROM for the duration of the test.

## Recording

```sh
./build/macos/ever2e profiles/apple2e.emu \
  --rom-file /absolute/path/to/APPLE2E.ROM \
  --headless \
  --paste-file samples/quick_flip.bas \
  --steps 20000000 \
  --record-video build/recordings/quick_flip_headless.mkv
```

`--record-video` writes a Matroska file with FFV1 video and signed 16-bit mono
PCM audio when FFmpeg support is available.

## Cleanup

Generated files live under `build/` and local-only assets under `local/`.

```sh
./scripts/macos/clean.sh
```

